mReport JSONL + summary. For the transport factory in dry-run, we could skip actual transports... but factory must succeed. In dry-run we could use a factory that constructs OpenRouterTransport from env — requires API key. Alternatively dry-run uses a factory that returns an error? No.\n\nAlternative: in dry-run, the CLI passes a factory returning a transport that never gets used — e.g., we can construct a transport without network... OpenRouterTransport::new(model, api_key) takes any strings, no validation probably. So dry-run factory: `|m| Ok(Box::new(OpenRouterTransport::new(m, \"dry-run\")) as Box<dyn Transport>)`. No network — construction only. Then budget `|| false` → all absent. Report written. That's hermetic, no model calls, no network.\n\nBut wait — does trial running need wai binary etc.? With budget exhausted, no trials run. Good.\n\nLet me check from_env and OpenRouterTransport::new to confirm no network at construction.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now, the key CLI design question: how to run ablate with no network/no model calls in an end-to-end test.\\n\\nrun_ablation requires transport factories. The CLI's production factory is OpenRouterTransport::from_env. For a dry-run/no-network mode, we need a way to run without transports. Options:\\n\\n1. `--dry-run`: run the ablation with a budget closure that immediately returns false → all cells become RotationEvent::Absent → report written with absent cells and delta=None. That requires no transport calls at all... wait — does the factory get invoked before budget check? In run_rotation_with_arm: `let mut transport = transport_factory(model)?;` happens BEFORE the budget check. So the factory is invoked per model even in dry-run. Hmm. With OpenRouterTransport::from_env, that reads OPENROUTER_API_KEY env var — no network on construction presumably (from_env just reads env). Let me check from_env: line 284. It probably reads env var and errors if missing — no network. Construction doesn't make network calls; only complete() does. So a dry-run where budget is exhausted from the start would construct transports (needs API key in env... error if absent, loud) but never call complete().\\n\\nHmm, but test with no API key: factory would fail loudly. Options for CLI:\\n\\n- Accept a `--registry <path>` flag? Brief says \\\"use an empty/absent registry path or a mock\\\". Interesting — suggests the CLI takes a model registry path argument. Maybe there's an env-configurable registry? Let me check registry.rs — REGISTRY is a static const. No path.\\n\\nMaybe the CLI ablate subcommand should accept `--models` or read registry from a path. The brief: \\\"runs the A/B ablation over the configured model registry\\\". \\\"configured\\\" — maybe registry.rs has env override? Let me read registry.rs fully.\\n\\nAlso \\\"dry-run\\\" idea: add a `--dry-run` flag where budget is `|| false` → everything absent; writes ArmReport JSONL + summary. For the transport factory in dry-run, we could skip actual transports... but factory must succeed. In dry-run we could use a factory that constructs OpenRouterTransport from env — requires API key. Alternatively dry-run uses a factory that returns an error? No.\\n\\nAlternative: in dry-run, the CLI passes a factory returning a transport that never gets used — e.g., we can construct a transport without network... OpenRouterTransport::new(model, api_key) takes any strings, no validation probably. So dry-run factory: `|m| Ok(Box::new(OpenRouterTransport::new(m, \\\"dry-run\\\")) as Box<dyn Transport>)`. No network — construction only. Then budget `|| false` → all absent. Report written. That's hermetic, no model calls, no network.\\n\\nBut wait — does trial running need wai binary etc.? With budget exhausted, no trials run. Good.\\n\\nLet me check from_env and OpenRouterTransport::new to confirm no network at construction.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4684b3f15b824261bdc432f1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n 263,300p /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/src/live.rs; echo ---; sed -n 1,60p /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/src/registry.rs","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1911,"output":710,"cacheRead":20736,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":629,"totalTokens":23357,"cost":{"input":0.00028665,"output":0.000355,"cacheRead":0.0006220799999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0012637299999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792435546002,"responseId":"gen-1792435546-QDZxR7jrSBdfQVxdQBBn","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
