port JSONL + summary. For the transport factory in dry-run, we could skip actual transports... but factory must succeed. In dry-run we could use a factory that constructs OpenRouterTransport from env — requires API key. Alternatively dry-run uses a factory that returns an error? No.\n\nAlternative: in dry-run, the CLI passes a factory returning a transport that never gets used — e.g., we can construct a transport without network... OpenRouterTransport::new(model, api_key) takes any strings, no validation probably. So dry-run factory: `|m| Ok(Box::new(OpenRouterTransport::new(m, \"dry-run\")) as Box<dyn Transport>)`. No network — construction only. Then budget `|| false` → all absent. Report written. That's hermetic, no model calls, no network.\n\nBut wait — does trial running need wai binary etc.? With budget exhausted, no trials run. Good.\n\nLet me check from_env and OpenRouterTransport::new to confirm no network at construction.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now, the key CLI design question: how to run ablate with no network/no model calls in an end-to-end test.\\n\\nrun_ablation requires transport factories. The CLI's production factory is OpenRouterTransport::from_env. For a dry-run/no-network mode, we need a way to run without transports. Options:\\n\\n1. `--dry-run`: run the ablation with a budget closure that immediately returns false → all cells become RotationEvent::Absent → report written with absent cells and delta=None. That requires no transport calls at all... wait — does the factory get invoked before budget check? In run_rotation_with_arm: `let mut transport = transport_factory(model)?;` happens BEFORE the budget check. So the factory is invoked per model even in dry-run. Hmm. With OpenRouterTransport::from_env, that reads OPENROUTER_API_KEY env var — no network on construction presumably (from_env just reads env). Let me check from_env: line 284. It probably reads env var and errors if missing — no network. Construction doesn't make network calls; only complete() does. So a dry-run where budget is exhausted from the start would construct transports (needs API key in env... error if absent, loud) but never call complete().\\n\\nHmm, but test with no API key: factory would fail loudly. Options for CLI:\\n\\n- Accept a `--registry <path>` flag? Brief says \\\"use an empty/absent registry path or a mock\\\". Interesting — suggests the CLI takes a model registry path argument. Maybe there's an env-configurable registry? Let me check registry.rs — REGISTRY is a static const. No path.\\n\\nMaybe the CLI ablate subcommand should accept `--models` or read registry from a path. The brief: \\\"runs the A/B ablation over the configured model registry\\\". \\\"configured\\\" — maybe registry.rs has env override? Let me read registry.rs fully.\\n\\nAlso \\\"dry-run\\\" idea: add a `--dry-run` flag where budget is `|| false` → everything absent; writes ArmReport JSONL + summary. For the transport factory in dry-run, we could skip actual transports... but factory must succeed. In dry-run we could use a factory that constructs OpenRouterTransport from env — requires API key. Alternatively dry-run uses a factory that returns an error? No.\\n\\nAlternative: in dry-run, the CLI passes a factory returning a transport that never gets used — e.g., we can construct a transport without network... OpenRouterTransport::new(model, api_key) takes any strings, no validation probably. So dry-run factory: `|m| Ok(Box::new(OpenRouterTransport::new(m, \\\"dry-run\\\")) as Box<dyn Transport>)`. No network — construction only. Then budget `|| false` → all absent. Report written. That's hermetic, no model calls, no network.\\n\\nBut wait — does trial running need wai binary etc.? With budget exhausted, no trials run. Good.\\n\\nLet me check from_env and OpenRouterTransport::new to confirm no network at construction.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4684b3f15b824261bdc432f1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n 263,300p /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/src/live.rs; echo ---; sed -n 1,60p /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/src/registry.rs","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1911,"output":710,"cacheRead":20736,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":629,"totalTokens":23357,"cost":{"input":0.00028665,"output":0.000355,"cacheRead":0.0006220799999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0012637299999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792435546002,"responseId":"gen-1792435546-QDZxR7jrSBdfQVxdQBBn","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4684b3f15b824261bdc432f1","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"pub struct OpenRouterTransport {\n    agent: ureq::Agent,\n    api_key: String,\n    model: String,\n}\n\nimpl OpenRouterTransport {\n    /// Build a transport for one model cell.\n    pub fn new(model: impl Into<String>, api_key: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            agent: ureq::AgentBuilder::new()\n                .timeout_connect(Duration::from_secs(10))\n                .build(),\n            api_key: api_key.into(),\n            model: model.into(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Build from the environment; the harness refuses to start tier-2\n    /// trials without a key (the anti-goal is silent degradation, not a\n    /// hidden key).\n    pub fn from_env(model: impl Into<String>) -> Result<Self, String> {\n        let key = std::env::var(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\").map_err(|_| {\n            \"OPENROUTER_API_KEY is not set — tier-2 live trials require it\".to_owned()\n        })?;\n        Ok(Self::new(model, key))\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Transport for OpenRouterTransport {\n    fn complete(&mut self, messages: &[Message]) -> Result<String, TransportError> {\n        let body = serde_json::json!({\n            \"model\": self.model,\n            \"messages\": messages\n                .iter()\n                .map(|m| serde_json::json!({\"role\": m.role, \"content\": m.content}))\n                .collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n        });\n---\n//! Purpose: Ordered model registry for tier-2 live trials.\n//! Responsibilities: hold the checked-in ordered registry of model ids\n//! with OpenRouter `:free` ids as the default first candidates, expose\n//! them verbatim, and define the repetition policy per scenario × model\n//! cell. The default first candidate is OpenRouter's free-models router\n//! (`openrouter/free`), which routes to its current free catalog.\n//! Rationale: evals-guidelines free-tier entry and attribution — the\n//! ordering defines scheduling priority (which cells run first), not\n//! failover; model fallback is a caller-level decision that must be\n//! recorded. Ids are never normalized because matrix comparisons across\n//! time depend on the raw id, including the `:free` suffix.\n\n/// One registry entry: a raw model id, verbatim.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct RegistryEntry {\n    /// The model id exactly as reported by the provider, including the\n    /// `:free` suffix when applicable.\n    pub id: &'static str,\n    /// Whether this entry is an OpenRouter free-tier id. Free ids sort\n    /// first in the registry ordering.\n    pub free: bool,\n}\n\n/// The checked-in ordered registry. `:free` ids first (scheduling\n/// priority), paid ids after. Nothing is special-cased beyond ordering.\npub const REGISTRY: &[RegistryEntry] = &[\n    RegistryEntry {\n        id: \"openrouter/free\",\n        free: true,\n    },\n    RegistryEntry {\n        id: \"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash:free\",\n        free: true,\n    },\n    RegistryEntry {\n        id: \"qwen/qwen3-coder:free\",\n        free: true,\n    },\n    RegistryEntry {\n        id: \"meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free\",\n        free: true,\n    },\n];\n\n/// Default repetitions per scenario × model cell (n>=3 by policy).\npub const DEFAULT_REPETITIONS: u32 = 3;\n\n/// Registry ids in scheduling order, verbatim.\npub fn ordered_ids() -> Vec<&'static str> {\n    REGISTRY.iter().map(|e| e.id).collect()\n}\n\n/// The free-tier entries, in registry order.\npub fn free_ids() -> Vec<&'static str> {\n    REGISTRY.iter().filter(|e| e.free).map(|e| e.id).collect()\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792435586908}]}
