{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":901,"output":1528,"cacheRead":23296,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1482,"totalTokens":25725,"cost":{"input":0.00013515,"output":0.0007639999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0006988799999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0015980299999999998}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Registry is static const; no path-based registry. The brief's \"empty/absent registry path or a mock\" — hmm. Maybe the intended dry-run: with no OPENROUTER_API_KEY and a budget already exhausted, transports are constructed but... from_env fails without key. So dry-run factory could be `|m| Ok(Box::new(OpenRouterTransport::new(m, \"dry-run\")))` — no key needed, no network unless complete() is called. Combined with `--dry-run` flag setting budget to `|| false` (zero budget → all cells absent). Report JSONL + summary written. Delta None.\n\nDesign of the `ablate` subcommand:\n\n```\n/// A/B ablation (evals.md Step 5) ...\nAblate {\n    /// Scenario name (a live battery scenario).\n    scenario: String,\n    /// Repetitions per arm (≥3, the evals.md delta floor).\n    #[arg(long, default_value_t = DEFAULT_REPETITIONS)]\n    reps: u32,\n    /// Run only this model id (default: whole registry in order).\n    #[arg(long, default_value = None)]\n    model: Option<String>,\n    /// Dry-run: no model calls — every cell is recorded absent and\n    /// the report shape is exercised end to end.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    dry_run: bool,\n    /// Write the per-arm rows as ArmReport JSONL to this path...\n    #[arg(long, default_value = None)]\n    out: Option<String>,\n}\n```\n\nBrief desired outcome: \"writes an ArmReport JSONL + summary\". So output: JSONL file of per-arm rows (RotationEvents are ArmReport rows — arm recorded additively on tier-2 rows, report_version 1) + summary (AblationReport serialized, maybe printed to stdout pretty like other commands).\n\nHmm, wait — but the budget closure: in dry-run, budget_remaining returns false always → cells absent. But the factory still constructs one transport per model — fine with OpenRouterTransport::new (fake key). But without dry_run, factory = from_env requiring OPENROUTER_API_KEY — loud error, good.\n\nAlso, dry-run still should error loudly on unknown scenario/registry: live_scenario_by_name errors loudly. Good.\n\nOutput files: \"writes an ArmReport JSONL + summary\". Let's design: `--out <dir or prefix>`? Keep simple: `--out <path>` where path is a JSONL file for the rows; summary printed to stdout (JSON pretty). Or write both files: `<out>.jsonl` rows and `<out>-summary.json`. Brief: \"writes the report files with ArmReport schema fields\". Test should check report files contain ArmReport schema fields: arm field, report_version 1, etc. RotationEvent::Trial serializes with arm + report (TrialReport has report_version presumably). Let me check RotationEvent serialization & TrialReport fields, and check the ablation tests for how they assert arm fields — \"arm recorded additively on tier-2 rows (report_version 1 unchanged)\".\n\nSimplest robust design honoring brief: CLI writes one JSONL file of rotation events (rows), each Trial row carrying `arm` and inner `report.report_version = 1`, plus prints the ablation summary (AblationReport with full/ablated ArmSummary, delta) to stdout. Files written: rows JSONL. \"ArmReport JSONL + summary\" — summary could be the stdout pretty JSON. For test assertions, capture stdout JSON as summary and read JSONL file for rows.\n\nAlternatively write two files: rows.jsonl and summary.json next to it. I'll do: `--out <path.jsonl>` writes rows JSONL; summary printed to stdout as pretty JSON. Test checks stdout summary fields (ablation_version, scenario, full, ablated, delta) and file rows fields (arm, report.report_version).\n\nActually \"writes an ArmReport JSONL + summary\" — to be safe, write summary to `<stem>-summary.json` next to the JSONL too? Keep simpler: stdout summary + JSONL file. Hmm, test in temp sandbox: run binary with args, capture stdout, assert. And assert file exists with rows. I think stdout summary is fine and consistent with `report` subcommand printing dashboard to stdout.\n\nWait, but there's `Command::Report` naming collision style... `Ablate` variant fine.\n\nAlso the ablation runs both arms; in dry-run all absent → ArmSummary trials=0, pass_rate None, delta None. JSONL rows: all Absent events with arm field. Check RotationEvent serialization: `#[serde(tag=...)]`? Let me check lines 179-260 of live.rs.\n\nAlso need to confirm what \"budget\" arg to add — maybe reuse budget concept? In non-dry-run mode, budget_mins like live. Add `--budget-mins` default 20 like live. Dry-run overrides budget to zero.\n\nAlso reps floor: run_ablation enforces ≥3 loudly. Good — test could also check loud error on reps<3? Keep brief: bad paths loud errors. Test scenario unknown name → exit nonzero with loud error message. Also bad out path (unwritable) → loud error.\n\nTest plan (tests/ablate_cli.rs), using env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\"):\n\n1. `ablate --help` → exit 0, stdout contains \"scenario\" arg name and \"ablate\". Actually clap help output: subcommand help `evallerina ablate --help` shows positional `scenario`. Test: run `<bin> ablate --help`, assert status success, stdout contains \"scenario\".\n\nWait brief step 1 RED: `evallerina ablate --help` exits 0 and names the scenario arg. Test via std::process::Command.\n\n2. Step 2 RED: end-to-end dry-run: temp sandbox dir, run `<bin> ablate wai-hint-adherence-smoke --dry-run --out <tmp>/rows.jsonl`, assert exit 0, stdout summary JSON parses with ablation_version=1, scenario name, full/ablated arm summaries, delta null, absent counts = 2 arms × registry models? Wait — registry is 4 models × 3 reps × 1 scenario = 12 cells per arm, 24 absent rows. But models come from registry regardless. Fine. Assert rows.jsonl lines each parse, each has \"arm\" field, Trial rows would have report_version — all absent here. Assert a