{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have everything I need. Design the CLI:\n\n```rust\n/// A/B ablation over the live battery scenario (evals.md Step 5): the\n/// full arm (AIX artifacts) vs the ablated arm, ≥3 reps per arm...\nAblate {\n    /// Scenario name (a live battery scenario; `--list`? no).\n    scenario: String,\n    #[arg(long, default_value_t = DEFAULT_REPETITIONS)]\n    reps: u32,\n    #[arg(long, default_value = None)]\n    model: Option<String>,\n    /// Dry-run: record every cell absent — no model calls, no network;\n    /// exercises the full report path hermetically.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    dry_run: bool,\n    /// Write the per-arm rotation rows as JSONL to this path.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    out: String,  // required? Brief: \"writes an ArmReport JSONL + summary\". Make it required.\n}\n```\n\nHmm — dry-run still constructs OpenRouterTransport with fake key via OpenRouterTransport::new. Actually wait: in dry-run, can we avoid needing transports at all? run_rotation_with_arm calls transport_factory(model)? before budget check, so factory must succeed. Using OpenRouterTransport::new(m, \"dry-run-no-network\") is fine — ureq agent construction makes no request.\n\nBut is a dry-run factory a \"modification of behavior in live.rs\"? No — we do it in main.rs. Good, no ablation.rs/live.rs changes.\n\nAlso dry-run should arguably not require OPENROUTER_API_KEY — right, we bypass from_env.\n\nSummary printing: pretty JSON of AblationReport to stdout. Rows: write each event JSON line to out file. Loud error if out path unwritable: write error mapped to Err(msg).\n\nNow run_ablation call in main.rs:\n\n```rust\nfn run_ablate(scenario: &str, reps: u32, model: Option<String>, dry_run: bool, out: &str) -> Result<ExitCode, String> {\n    let scenario = evallerina::scenario::live_scenario_by_name(scenario)?;\n    let models: Vec<String> = match model {\n        Some(id) => vec![id],\n        None => ordered_ids().into_iter().map(String::from).collect(),\n    };\n    let report = evallerina::ablation::run_ablation(\n        &scenario,\n        &models,\n        reps,\n        evallerina::ablation::AixSource::Static(&DEFAULT_AIX_ARTIFACTS),\n        evallerina::ablation::AblationFactories { full: ..., ablated: ... },\n        &evallerina::live::Bounds::default(),\n        &budget,\n    )?;\n```\n\nWait — artifacts: production wires the real generated artifacts (opt-in flag from evallerina-0j8). Brief: \"wire run_ablation from src/ablation.rs including the real-generation opt-in flag from evallerina-0j8\". So CLI needs a flag to opt into real generation: e.g. `--real-artifacts` (uses AixSource::Real with ToolBinaries::discover_wai(), loud error if wai absent). Default: Static(&DEFAULT_AIX_ARTIFACTS) — but AixArtifacts requires &'static str contents; production static contents... The test_artifacts in tests are test content. For the CLI default static, what contents? Hmm. There's no production static artifact set. Options: make the CLI default to real generation? No — real generation is opt-in (0j8). Default static could reuse... hmm.\n\nMaybe simplest: CLI artifact flag with three modes: default static (test/dulce placeholder contents defined in main.rs?), or is that wrong? Let me check how tests/ablation.rs uses AixSource and whether there's a canonical production static set anywhere. Also check GeneratedAixArtifacts usage and llms_txt constant maybe in scenario.rs. Let me grep for AixSource usage.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now I have everything I need. Design the CLI:\\n\\n```rust\\n/// A/B ablation over the live battery scenario (evals.md Step 5): the\\n/// full arm (AIX artifacts) vs the ablated arm, ≥3 reps per arm...\\nAblate {\\n    /// Scenario name (a live battery scenario; `--list`? no).\\n    scenario: String,\\n    #[arg(long, default_value_t = DEFAULT_REPETITIONS)]\\n    reps: u32,\\n    #[arg(long, default_value = None)]\\n    model: Option<String>,\\n    /// Dry-run: record every cell absent — no model calls, no network;\\n    /// exercises the full report path hermetically.\\n    #[arg(long)]\\n    dry_run: bool,\\n    /// Write the per-arm rotation rows as JSONL to this path.\\n    #[arg(long)]\\n    out: String,  // required? Brief: \\\"writes an ArmReport JSONL + summary\\\". Make it required.\\n}\\n```\\n\\nHmm — dry-run still constructs OpenRouterTransport with fake key via OpenRouterTransport::new. Actually wait: in dry-run, can we avoid needing transports at all? run_rotation_with_arm calls transport_factory(model)? before budget check, so factory must succeed. Using OpenRouterTransport::new(m, \\\"dry-run-no-network\\\") is fine — ureq agent construction makes no request.\\n\\nBut is a dry-run factory a \\\"modification of behavior in live.rs\\\"? No — we do it in main.rs. Good, no ablation.rs/live.rs changes.\\n\\nAlso dry-run should arguably not require OPENROUTER_API_KEY — right, we bypass from_env.\\n\\nSummary printing: pretty JSON of AblationReport to stdout. Rows: write each event JSON line to out file. Loud error if out path unwritable: write error mapped to Err(msg).\\n\\nNow run_ablation call in main.rs:\\n\\n```rust\\nfn run_ablate(scenario: &str, reps: u32, model: Option<String>, dry_run: bool, out: &str) -> Result<ExitCode, String> {\\n    let scenario = evallerina::scenario::live_scenario_by_name(scenario)?;\\n    let models: Vec<String> = match model {\\n        Some(id) => vec![id],\\n        None => ordered_ids().into_iter().map(String::from).collect(),\\n    };\\n    let report = evallerina::ablation::run_ablation(\\n        &scenario,\\n        &models,\\n        reps,\\n        evallerina::ablation::AixSource::Static(&DEFAULT_AIX_ARTIFACTS),\\n        evallerina::ablation::AblationFactories { full: ..., ablated: ... },\\n        &evallerina::live::Bounds::default(),\\n        &budget,\\n    )?;\\n```\\n\\nWait — artifacts: production wires the real generated artifacts (opt-in flag from evallerina-0j8). Brief: \\\"wire run_ablation from src/ablation.rs including the real-generation opt-in flag from evallerina-0j8\\\". So CLI needs a flag to opt into real generation: e.g. `--real-artifacts` (uses AixSource::Real with ToolBinaries::discover_wai(), loud error if wai absent). Default: Static(&DEFAULT_AIX_ARTIFACTS) — but AixArtifacts requires &'static str contents; production static contents... The test_artifacts in tests are test content. For the CLI default static, what contents? Hmm. There's no production static artifact set. Options: make the CLI default to real generation? No — real generation is opt-in (0j8). Default static could reuse... hmm.\\n\\nMaybe simplest: CLI artifact flag with three modes: default static (test/dulce placeholder contents defined in main.rs?), or is that wrong? Let me check how tests/ablation.rs uses AixSource and whether there's a canonical production static set anywhere. Also check GeneratedAixArtifacts usage and llms_txt constant maybe in scenario.rs. Let me grep for AixSource usage.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_15524ea92e1840ccb1fa3f41","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"rg -n \"AixSource|ToolBinaries|discover_wai|AixArtifacts\" /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/src /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/tests | grep -v \"^.*ablation.rs:\" ; echo ===; rg -n \"AixSource\" /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/tests/ablation.rs","timeout":30}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2440e43472d645ed83d0fc8e","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n 151,260p /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/tests/ablation.rs","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":895,"output":1000,"cacheRead":25600,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":832,"totalTokens":27495,"cost":{"input":0.00013424999999999998,"output":0.0005,"cacheRead":0.0007679999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0014022499999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792435662213,"responseId":"gen-1792435662-tDmkZIGMaA2yXXpDfIHr","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_15524ea92e1840ccb1fa3f41","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"===\n23:    AblationFactories, AixArtifacts, AixSource, ToolBinaries, run_ablation,\n249:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n299:        AixSource::Real(ToolBinaries { wai: failing }),\n348:        AixSource::Real(ToolBinaries { wai: failing }),\n375:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n408:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n429:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n455:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n482:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n529:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n555:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n604:        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792435689340},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2440e43472d645ed83d0fc8e","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/// managed block markers from genesis-vibes, never placeholder text.\n/// Skips hermetically when no `wai` binary is available (CI without\n/// tool binaries); runs for real wherever the tool is provisioned.\n#[test]\nfn real_generation_writes_managed_agents_md_with_wai_provenance() {\n    let Some(wai) = ToolBinaries::discover_wai() else {\n        return; // no tool binaries provisioned → hermetic skip\n    };\n    let dir = unique_dir(\"real-agents-md\");\n    let generated =\n        AixArtifacts::for_fixture(&dir, &ToolBinaries { wai }).expect(\"wai init generates\");\n    let block = BlockDef::new(\"WAI\");\n    assert!(\n        generated.managed_agents_md.contains(&block.start_marker),\n        \"real AGENTS.md carries the managed block start marker\"\n    );\n    assert!(\n        generated.managed_agents_md.contains(&block.end_marker),\n        \"real AGENTS.md carries the managed block end marker\"\n    );\n    assert!(\n        generated\n            .managed_agents_md\n            .contains(\"provenance: generator=wai\"),\n        \"real AGENTS.md carries wai's provenance footer\"\n    );\n    assert!(\n        !generated.managed_agents_md.contains(\"managed guidance\"),\n        \"real AGENTS.md is never the placeholder text\"\n    );\n    // wai init also registers the tool manifest via genesis discovery:\n    // the produced `.genesis/tools.toml` is the real registered one.\n    assert!(\n        generated.tools_toml.contains(\"[tools.wai]\"),\n        \"real tools.toml registers wai: {}\",\n        generated.tools_toml\n    );\n    std::fs::remove_dir_all(&dir).ok();\n}\n\n/// Real generation: the fixture's `llms.txt` is the genesis-vibes\n/// `generate_llms_txt` output for the fixture tool set — title, module\n/// section markers, and the registered tool entries, never placeholder\n/// text. Runs for real wherever the tool is provisioned.\n#[test]\nfn real_generation_llms_txt_is_genesis_output_for_the_tool_set() {\n    let Some(wai) = ToolBinaries::discover_wai() else {\n        return; // no tool binaries provisioned → hermetic skip\n    };\n    let dir = unique_dir(\"real-llms-txt\");\n    let generated =\n        AixArtifacts::for_fixture(&dir, &ToolBinaries { wai }).expect(\"wai init generates\");\n    // The standardized concise format: `# {project}` title and the\n    // module listing of the registered fixture tool set.\n    assert!(\n        generated.llms_txt.starts_with(\"# \"),\n        \"llms.txt carries the project title: {}\",\n        generated.llms_txt\n    );\n    assert!(\n        generated.llms_txt.contains(\"## Modules\"),\n        \"llms.txt carries the module section marker: {}\",\n        generated.llms_txt\n    );\n    assert!(\n        generated.llms_txt.contains(\"`wai`\"),\n        \"llms.txt lists the registered tool: {}\",\n        generated.llms_txt\n    );\n    assert!(\n        !generated.llms_txt.contains(\"wai status --json\"),\n        \"llms.txt is never the placeholder text\"\n    );\n    std::fs::remove_dir_all(&dir).ok();\n}\n\n// ── hermetic fallback (opt-out / no tool binaries) ─────────────────────────\n\n/// Without the real-generation opt-in (no tool binaries provisioned,\n/// or the caller simply doesn't opt in) the harness stays hermetic:\n/// the full arm provisions exactly today's static contents — behavior\n/// byte-for-byte unchanged.\n#[test]\nfn static_source_provisions_hermetic_contents_unchanged() {\n    let static_md = test_artifacts().managed_agents_md;\n    let scenario =\n        Scenario::new(\"hermetic-probe\", \"create the file\").check(\"agents-md-is-static\", move |r| {\n            let md = std::fs::read_to_string(r.fixture_root.join(\"AGENTS.md\")).unwrap_or_default();\n            if md == static_md {\n                CheckOutcome::pass()\n            } else {\n                CheckOutcome::tool_fault(\"AGENTS.md is not the hermetic static content\")\n            }\n        });\n    let report = run_ablation(\n        &scenario,\n        &[\"m1\".to_owned()],\n        3,\n        AixSource::Static(&test_artifacts()),\n        AblationFactories {\n            full: &mut green_factory(),\n            ablated: &mut green_factory(),\n        },\n        &Bounds::default(),\n        &always_open,\n    )\n    .expect(\"ablation runs\");\n    assert_eq!(report.full.passed, 3, \"full arm sees the static contents\");\n    assert_eq!(report.ablated.failed, 3, \"ablated arm sees none of them\");\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792435689340}]}
