on! mapping fields. Let me just print the full AblationReport pretty — \"the report is auditable, not a black box\", and the rows file is the JSONL. Duplication acceptable? The summary on stdout would be big. Better: print summary-only JSON:\n\n```rust\nlet summary = serde_json::json!({\n    \"ablation_version\": report.ablation_version,\n    \"scenario\": report.scenario,\n    \"full\": report.full,\n    \"ablated\": report.ablated,\n    \"delta\": report.delta,\n});\nprintln!(\"{}\", serde_json::to_string_pretty(&summary).unwrap());\n```\n\nGood — that's \"ArmReport JSONL + summary\".\n\nExit code: success always if it ran? Ablation is measurement; findings don't gate. Exit SUCCESS. Errors loud.\n\nCheck TransportFactory definition quickly, then write test file. Also need `writeln` import. In tests: e2e asserts:\n\n- run `ablate wai-hint-adherence-smoke --dry-run --out rows.jsonl` in sandbox; success.\n- stdout parses as JSON summary; ablation_version == 1; scenario name; full.absent == 12 (4 models × 3 reps); ablated.absent == 12; delta null.\n- rows.jsonl: 24 lines, each kind == \"absent\", arm full/ablated (12 each).\n\nWait — dry-run also must not require OPENROUTER_API_KEY. Test environment: cargo test may inherit env... ensure no key needed (fake key). Also ensure env doesn't have wai needed — no trials run.\n\nAlso `--reps` default 3 ≥ floor. In dry-run with reps<3? run_ablation floor check happens first — loud error. Fine.\n\nLoud-error test: unknown scenario → nonzero exit + stderr contains \"unknown scenario\". Also bad out path (e.g. out into nonexistent dir) → nonzero, stderr mentions \"cannot write\". Add both as part of step 2 (loud errors anti-goal).\n\nStep-1 test: `ablate --help` exit 0, stdout contains \"scenario\" and \"--dry-run\"? Brief: \"names the scenario arg\". Also test that `ablate` with unknown scenario fails loudly? That's step 2 territory.\n\nTest count: keep tight: \n1. help test (step 1)\n2. dry-run e2e (step 2)\n3. unknown scenario