Name":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# evallerina — eval battery for the dulce-de-leche tool family\n# Tier ladder per genesis evals-guidelines: 0 static (push) / 1 replay (nightly) / 2 live (scheduled)\n\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# Tier 0 — static checks, no model (gates every push)\ntier0:\n    cargo fmt --check\n    cargo clippy -- -D warnings\n    cargo test\n\n# Tier 1 — scripted replay of recorded AgentStep transcripts, no model, no network\ntier1:\n    cargo test --test evals_replay -- --nocapture\n\n# Tier 2 — live rotation (requires OPENROUTER_API_KEY); never gates a push.\n# One JSON event per cell on stdout (trial row or absent record).\ntier2 model=\"openrouter/free\" scenario=\"\" budget=\"20\":\n    #!/usr/bin/env bash\n    set -euo pipefail\n    args=(live --model \"{{model}}\" --budget-mins \"{{budget}}\")\n    if [ -n \"{{scenario}}\" ]; then args+=(\"{{scenario}}\"); fi\n    cargo run --release -- \"${args[@]}\"\n\n# Build + test the harness crate\nci: tier0\n\n# Fixture sandbox smoke test: provision binaries, run one replay scenario\nsmoke:\n    cargo run --release -- smoke\n===\nablation.rs\nevals_replay.rs\nlive_protocol.rs\nreport_aggregation.rs\nrouting.rs\n/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/tests/report_aggregation.rs:509:    let out = std::process::Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\"))\n/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/tests/report_aggregation.rs:572:    let out = std::process::Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\"))\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792435731463},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d9e32c26660da2b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n 480,600p /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/tests/report_aggregation.rs","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1605,"output":48,"cacheRead":28160,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":29813,"cost":{"input":0.00024075,"output":0.000024,"cacheRead":0.0008447999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00110955}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792435731465,"responseId":"gen-1792435731-pf6qPpMpanUKHUUGqWfY","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9d9e32c26660da2b","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"}\n\n/// End-to-end CLI contract: `evallerina report rows.jsonl` WITHOUT\n/// --route carries no `routed` field and writes no jsonl — routing is\n/// strictly opt-in, the dashboard is unchanged.\n#[test]\nfn report_without_route_has_no_routed_field_and_no_jsonl() {\n    let sandbox = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\n        \"evallerina-o3j-noroute-{}-{}\",\n        std::process::id(),\n        std::time::SystemTime::now()\n            .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)\n            .unwrap()\n            .as_nanos()\n    ));\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(&sandbox).expect(\"create sandbox\");\n    let rows = json!({\n        \"kind\": \"trial\",\n        \"report_version\": 1,\n        \"scenario\": \"wai-hint-adherence-typo\",\n        \"tool\": \"wai\",\n        \"status\": \"failed\",\n        \"checks\": [{\"name\": \"check-b\", \"passed\": false, \"reason\": \"envelope missing\"}],\n        \"model\": \"m1\",\n        \"repetition\": 0\n    })\n    .to_string();\n    std::fs::write(sandbox.join(\"rows.jsonl\"), rows).expect(\"write rows\");\n\n    let out = std::process::Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\"))\n        .args([\"report\", \"rows.jsonl\"])\n        .current_dir(&sandbox)\n        .output()\n        .expect(\"run report\");\n    assert!(out.status.success());\n    let dashboard: serde_json::Value =\n        serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).expect(\"dashboard JSON on stdout\");\n    assert!(\n        dashboard.get(\"routed\").is_none(),\n        \"no routed field without --route\"\n    );\n    assert!(\n        !sandbox.join(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\").exists(),\n        \"no proposed-tickets.jsonl without --route\"\n    );\n\n    std::fs::remove_dir_all(&sandbox).ok();\n}\n\n/// End-to-end CLI contract: `evallerina report rows.jsonl --route`\n/// prints a dashboard whose `routed` summary has dry_run > 0, keeps\n/// report_version 1, and writes proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the\n/// report. Runs in a temp sandbox with a copy of routing.toml so no\n/// tracked file or family repo is touched.\n#[test]\nfn report_route_dry_run_writes_proposed_tickets_jsonl() {\n    let sandbox = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\n        \"evallerina-o3j-route-{}-{}\",\n        std::process::id(),\n        std::time::SystemTime::now()\n            .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)\n            .unwrap()\n            .as_nanos()\n    ));\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(&sandbox).expect(\"create sandbox\");\n    std::fs::copy(\n        concat!(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"), \"/routing.toml\"),\n        sandbox.join(\"routing.toml\"),\n    )\n    .expect(\"copy routing.toml into sandbox\");\n    let rows = [\"m1\", \"m2\", \"m3\"]\n        .iter()\n        .map(|m| {\n            json!({\n                \"kind\": \"trial\",\n                \"report_version\": 1,\n                \"scenario\": \"wai-hint-adherence-typo\",\n                \"tool\": \"wai\",\n                \"status\": \"failed\",\n                \"checks\": [{\"name\": \"check-b\", \"passed\": false, \"reason\": \"envelope missing\"}],\n                \"model\": m,\n                \"repetition\": 0\n            })\n        })\n        .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n        .iter()\n        .map(serde_json::to_string)\n        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()\n        .unwrap()\n        .join(\"\\n\");\n    std::fs::write(sandbox.join(\"rows.jsonl\"), rows).expect(\"write rows\");\n\n    let out = std::process::Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\"))\n        .args([\"report\", \"rows.jsonl\", \"--route\"])\n        .current_dir(&sandbox)\n        .output()\n        .expect(\"run report --route\");\n    assert!(out.status.success(), \"report --route succeeds\");\n    let dashboard: serde_json::Value =\n        serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).expect(\"dashboard JSON on stdout\");\n    assert_eq!(dashboard[\"routed\"][\"dry_run\"], 1);\n    assert_eq!(dashboard[\"report_version\"], 1);\n\n    let jsonl = std::fs::read_to_string(sandbox.join(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\"))\n        .expect(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl written next to the report\");\n    let row: serde_json::Value = jsonl\n        .lines()\n        .next()\n        .map(|l| serde_json::from_str(l).unwrap())\n        .unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(\n        row[\"token\"],\n        \"evallerina:wai-hint-adherence-typo:tool_fault\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(row[\"decision\"], \"dry_run\");\n\n    std::fs::remove_dir_all(&sandbox).ok();\n}\n\n/// Routing failures surface as skipped counts, not errors: an unmapped\n/// tool (no routing.toml entry) yields a skipped proposal and the\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792435737101},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have the CLI test pattern. Now write the RED test first (tests/ablate_cli.rs), run it (fails: no `ablate` subcommand), then implement in main.rs, then GREEN, then step 2 red (e2e test) — wait, step 1 red is the --help test; step 2 red is the e2e dry-run test. Per brief: \n\n1. RED: help test → GREEN.\n2. RED: e2e dry-run test → GREEN.\n\nCommits atomic per green step.\n\nInteresting question about the serde tag of RotationEvent: from report_aggregation test, Trial rows serialize with \"kind\": \"trial\". Absent events presumably \"kind\": \"absent\". Let me confirm — line ~170 of live.rs. Quick grep.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"I have the CLI test pattern. Now write the RED test first (tests/ablate_cli.rs), run it (fails: no `ablate` subcommand), then implement in main.rs, then GREEN, then step 2 red (e2e test) — wait, step 1 red is the --help test; step 2 red is the e2